WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:33.970
Let's Go Camping!

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.870
So much stuff.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.790
Well, we are going camping.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:44.790
Camping <i>(kyanpu)</i>?

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.150
That would be a champ <i>(chanpu)</i>.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.150
That would be a slump <i>(suranpu)</i>.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.140
Those would be bagpipes <i>(bagupaipu)</i>.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.490
That would be bitter melon 
champloo <i>(goya champuru)</i>. {I don't know if "goya" is well known enough to not be translated?}

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.430
I've never been camping.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.180
When you go camping,

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.410
you sleep in total darkness 
out in the mountains,

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:12.150
alone and secluded on the cold, hard ground.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.770
Really?

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:19.680
So, you like quietly sleeping 
in dark places, Mr. Penguin?

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.950
No, I don't.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.800
Camping is when you're out in nature,

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.220
eating delicious food 
pitching a tent,

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:28.400
and gazing at all the pretty stars in the sky!

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:31.770
As long as there's bamboo grass or bamboo.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:35.210
That's no different 
from any other time.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.160
Grizzly will be here soon, too.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.680
Huh? Who's that?

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:42.780
He was here when we were weeding.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.140
Weeding?

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:47.600
Oh,

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.390
that bear that came in like, "rawr" 
and left like, "whoosh."

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.350
Hey, Polar Bear.

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.250
Good morning, Mr. Grizzly.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.770
You're coming along, too, Panda?

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.620
The hell is this small thing, a bird?

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:10.580
I'm a penguin!

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.540
You're so small,
I couldn't tell.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.500
Emperor penguins are the 
greatest among all penguins!

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.220
You're still smaller than a bear.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:24.920
Come on, let's go.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:30.090
That bear is really disrespectful.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.140
Mr. Grizzly doesn't think about what he says.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.110
I don't want to hear that from you.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:40.820
Danger!

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:40.820
Beware     of       Bears

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.780
It's nice and cool out.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:49.750
It feels great to be 
in the great outdoors!

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.820
All right!

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:56.710
First off...

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.920
Let's decide on who's 
in charge of the camp.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.250
Hey! Hey!

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.410
Don't jump in so abruptly!

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:05.180
Who cares who leads?

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:05.890
Right?

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.320
Hey!

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.690
What are you doing?

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:12.150
I'm reading a book in 
the great outdoors.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.470
Huh? What's going on?

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.890
Oh, is it already time to eat?

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:17.860
No, it's not.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:20.550
If we don't set up soon,

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.780
it's going to get dark.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.820
Yeah, let's get set up, Mr. Penguin.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.890
That's what we were just saying!

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:32.020
First, let's decide on 
who's in charge of what, Grizzly.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:35.060
That's what I was just saying!

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:38.160
What are we going to do first?

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.480
First, we have to pitch the tent.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.260
Then we can divide up the duties of

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:45.880
making a fire, preparing the food, 
and making the rice.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.290
Okay, wake me up when the food's ready.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.000
Hey!

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.590
You're helping, too, Panda.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:55.100
I am?

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:55.940
Yes, you are!

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:57.860
So, who's in charge of what?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.610
Good question...

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.980
Pitching the tent: everyone.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.610
Making the fire: Polar Bear.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.220
I'll prepare the food,

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.470
and the penguin will make the rice.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:08.700
Hey, don't just 
decide for everyone.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.120
Don't sweat the small stuff, bird.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.670
B-Bird?

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:15.080
Hey, what about me?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.010
You'll be something like the helper.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.800
Well, let's get the tent up first.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.040
The tent's ready!

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.240
No, it's not.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.720
That's not a tent!

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.180
All done.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.220
You're shining right now, Mr. Penguin,

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:40.100
even though you're usually so drab.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:44.150
Comments like that 
aren't needed, Panda.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:47.210
Well then, let's go inside.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:48.110
Yeah.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:56.000
It's too damn small!

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.890
It's not going to be possible 
for all of us to fit.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.730
What are we going 
to do, Polar Bear?!

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:02.610
I have a great idea.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.340
What are we going to do?

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:09.620
I brought another tent, 
so pitch it, too.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:10.770
You have another one?!

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.200
You should have told us earlier!

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:18.700
Well then, I'm going to prepare dinner.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:20.850
How's the firewood <i>(maki)</i> coming along?

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:23.450
That's a...

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:24.570
trout <i>(masu)</i>!

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.410
You need to collect firewood, 
not trout, Polar Bear!

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:30.090
You're in charge of making the fire!

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:42.590
Why can't everyone do what 
they're supposed to?

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.680
Got that right.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.740
Ow!

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.930
Hey, stop that!

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.650
You're making the fire spark!

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:59.600
Aw, but I worked so hard to get some.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.110
What the hell are you doing?!

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:02.930
Don't put a stump in there!

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.930
You're going to end up 
putting the fire out!

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:07.690
But I worked so hard to get it.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.450
What the hell is wrong with 
Polar Bear and Panda?

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.140
They're so troublesome.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:29.510
It smells so good.

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:32.610
What are you making?

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:33.710
Curry.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:35.430
It's a standard for camping.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.890
Oh, I know!

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.450
For the secret ingredient.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:42.190
Don't you dare put that in!

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.570
I can't imagine curry 
without bamboo grass...

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:46.860
There isn't any in normal curry!

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.910
Damn it, we can't let our 
guard down for a second.

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:54.220
Polar Bear!

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:57.530
We just said stop putting 
unnecessary things in there!

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:00.450
I thought we'd make it seafood curry.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.290
This isn't the sea.
 It's a lake.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.350
Hey, is something burning?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.930
It's all black.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:23.190
We watching those idiots
so much, we forgot.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:25.670
I'm sorry.

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:26.810
Don't worry about it.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:30.680
Hey! I brought flour.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:32.980
Well, since we're having curry,

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:34.490
how about we make some naan?

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.340
Okay.

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:02.480
It's so good.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:04.940
A great reward for all the 
hard work we put in.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:07.670
Wow, you're amazing, Polar Bear!

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:09.820
It's not pizza!

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:09.820
Hey, hey, hey!

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:15.320
Grizzly and I did most of the work.

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:17.310
Exactly.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:29.120
All right, it's ready.

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:31.240
I'm first!

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:32.920
You're later.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.180
Penguin, you go first.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:37.510
Huh?

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:46.080
You worked the hardest.

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:50.520
Thanks.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.190
How is it?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.490
How's the temperature?

00:09:55.330 --> 00:10:00.750
<i>Honestly, I'd prefer a cold 
bath instead of a hot one.</i>

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.440
It's just right.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:05.590
Good to hear.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:08.380
Well, warm up.

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:12.880
It feels nice.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:27.490
Well, how's the temperature?

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:29.690
It's boiling, Panda!

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.280
There's an ice bath, too.

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.690
You should have told me 
that first, Polar Bear!

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:42.570
Guess we should head to bed.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:43.600
In that case,

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:47.250
let's draw straws to decide
 who will share a tent.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.160
Everyone grab one each.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:54.970
Mine has a leaf!

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.220
The first tent will be 
Polar Bear and Panda.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:01.170
The other will be you and me.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:08.300
Thanks for all your hard work today.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.480
Same to you.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:12.690
It must be hard for you, too.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:14.320
Huh?

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:19.660
Not only do Polar Bear 
and Panda do nothing,

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:22.420
they cause more work 
for the rest of us.

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:24.440
Exactly.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:27.790
<u>Breakfast:</u>

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:27.790
I'm putting it in my curry, 
so don't eat it!!

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:27.300
They're so troublesome.

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:30.730
But you can't just...

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.830
...leave them alone.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:40.770
Want to drink?

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:42.820
I brought my special reserves.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:44.470
Sounds great!

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:48.110
We go through so much trouble!

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:50.560
Right, Penguin?

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.850
So true!

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:55.020
We can't watch after you 
guys all the time!

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:57.380
I want to scream!

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:58.980
Let's scream!

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.120
What are they doing?

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:08.830
That's really annoying.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:19.340
You'll catch a cold sleeping out here.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:24.950
Jeez, Mr. Penguin and Grizzly are so...

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.010
...troublesome, aren't they?

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:31.220
That would be...

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:34.330
the two of you!

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:42.950
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:41.700
Rin Rin and the High School Girl.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:44.590
Miss Sasako,

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:47.930
what purpose does the groove below humans' noses serve?

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:50.140
You know, I'm not really sure.

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:53.680
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:55.040
What is it, Panda?

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:59.710
You're always lazing around this café,

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:04.000
but you should try
 working like me sometime.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.720
How about I just say I'd rather 
not hear that from you?

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:11.000
Speaking of, don't you have work today?

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:12.630
It's this afternoon.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:15.320
It's really hard working 
two days a week,

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:17.430
so I said I'd be coming 
in the afternoon.

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:19.280
I'm amazed that you 
haven't been fired yet.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:23.150
Oh, you're here, Panda?

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.150
What?

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:26.950
Here you go.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:28.550
This is for you, Panda.

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:31.700
What?

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.190
Is it Panda Day today?

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.120
What kind of day is that?

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.320
Where'd you get this, Polar Bear?

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:38.770
A moment ago...

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:41.390
Please give this to Panda.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.340
...is what he asked me.

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:48.340
You can have it.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.200
Huh?

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:51.710
It's Rin Rin again.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:53.180
The florist?

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:53.810
Yeah.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:58.810
I wonder what he has against me.

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:01.020
He's just giving you flowers.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.970
I hope Panda liked those flowers.

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:07.450
Look! It's the florist!

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:09.410
Welcome.

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:11.330
Could I get this, please?

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.870
Excuse me, could I get this?

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:17.570
Thank you very much.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:27.240
<i>Mr. Rintarou is always so amazing.</i>

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:34.640
Can I help you?

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:37.250
No.

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:38.180
Um...

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:40.810
I'll come again.

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:46.970
Wait!

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:48.470
Yes?

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:52.910
Could we go somewhere together?

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.880
<i>W-W-W-W-What am I going to do?!</i>

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.820
<i>Mr. Rintarou just asked me out!</i>

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:02.540
<i>Is this a date?</i>

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.340
<i>W-W-W-W-What am I going to do?!</i>

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:07.350
<i>But, why me?</i>

00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:10.100
<i>There's all those other pretty girls.</i>

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:12.590
<i>Is it my plainness?</i>

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:16.750
Congratulations

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:16.770
<i>Could it be the plainness of being 
a high school student won out?</i>

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:20.740
<i>Wow, Mr. Rintarou asked me out.</i>

00:15:21.450 --> 00:15:22.320
Is it all right?

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:23.780
Can you go?

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:26.230
Yes!

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:29.820
<i>Since Mr. Rintarou has such good taste,</i>

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.200
<i>he must be taking me 
to a wonderful place.</i>

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:38.070
Look everyone, it's Mr. Elephant.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:41.000
Um...

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.090
What's wrong?

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:44.620
Oh, it was just a little unexpected.

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:47.050
Well then, let's go.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:49.670
Okay!

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:56.470
Um, Mr. Rintarou.

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:57.810
What is it?

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:00.430
Nevermind...

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.240
What is it?

00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:04.400
You can ask me anything.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.030
Um,

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:11.360
your girlfriend must be 
a wonderful person.

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.780
I don't have a girlfriend.

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:16.900
Oh, really?

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:17.790
Yep.

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:37.970
But there is someone I can't 
stop thinking about.

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.930
Could that be...

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:48.610
D-Does the age gap matter?

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:49.710
Age gap?

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:52.900
I never even thought about that.

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:54.540
Me neither!

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.240
What are they like?

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:02.870
Well, black and white looks 
really cute on them.

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:04.510
<i>My uniform?</i>

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:05.790
<i>He has a uniform fetish?</i>

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:08.560
<i>That's okay.</i>

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:10.570
<i>I'm totally okay with that.</i>

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:12.010
And they're fluffy...

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:14.720
<i>He must be talking about my pigtails!</i>

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:16.600
<i>Good job!</i>

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:18.290
<i>Good job, me!</i>

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:19.640
And they're chubby.

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:21.460
<i>It's the potato chips.</i>

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:23.270
<i>I ate too many potato chips!</i>

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:24.770
<i>You fail.</i>

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:26.100
<i>You fail, me.</i>

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:27.860
And they're so cute sprawled out.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:30.470
<i>Peeping?</i>

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:32.230
<i>Is he secretly taking photos of me?</i>

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:34.470
All that...

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.860
is why I love Panda so much.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:42.790
Panda?

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:44.620
Yes, Panda.

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:49.750
<i>Rin Rin's here again.</i>

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:50.670
And so,

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:53.260
could you take care of this for me?

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:57.470
Thank you so much!

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:00.630
That's the first time I took 
a picture with Panda.

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:03.360
I'm so happy you came with me.

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:04.700
It's nothing...

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:06.880
You like pandas, too, right?

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:08.440
I could totally tell by that.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.070
Those who like pandas can tell 
others who like pandas.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:14.460
Right?

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:16.960
<i>What's with this intensity?</i>

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:18.990
<i>Is this really Mr. Rintarou?</i>

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:21.080
<i>But...</i>

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:26.180
<i>if pandas get me closer to Mr. Rintarou...</i>

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:30.520
Wow, he's so cute!

00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:31.960
Wrong, wrong.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.730
The one that's cute 
isn't the panda there,

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:37.420
but Panda over there!

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:40.410
T-They're different?

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:42.390
Completely different.

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:46.350
Here, look carefully.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:50.400
Pay attention and look.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.360
O-Okay.

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:53.770
Mr. Panda there,

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:56.780
and Panda there.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:18:59.860
Mr. Panda there,

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:02.500
and Panda there.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:04.590
See?

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:12.170
<i>I can't tell the difference at all.</i>

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:15.540
<i>But...</i>

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:24.100
Um... that panda over 
there is much cuter.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:27.290
Right?!

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:29.330
You!

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:30.270
Yes?!

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:34.150
How about we spend another hour

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:36.280
talking about Panda's 
cuteness together?

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:38.170
Huh?

00:19:39.930 --> 00:19:41.590
He's so cute, isn't he?

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:43.680
Did you see his fluffy face?

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:45.020
I totally saw it!

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:46.200
What am I going to do?

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:48.620
Is there anything cuter?

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.180
No, there isn't!

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:51.850
If it was possible, I'd want to live

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:54.040
with Panda in the panda corner.

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:55.560
That'd be great.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:56.650
What would I do?

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:59.240
But Panda only works two days a week,

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:02.490
so anytime other than that...

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:01.130
<i>I want to go home.</i>

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:08.350
...Being able to see him cutely rolling 
around up close is so amazing, isn't it?

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.920
<i>I want to go home...</i>

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:10.860
Panda rolling around is great,

00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:14.520
but Panda sliding down his slide 
is totally cute, too, isn't it?

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.950
<i>We are now closed.</i>

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:18.840
<i>We look forward to your next visit.</i>

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:18.050
It's closing time.

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:21.490
I'm sorry, this ended 
up being really long.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:24.020
O-Oh, it's fine.

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:27.870
<i>Saved.</i>

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.020
Well then...

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:29.950
Yes.

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:33.920
Let's go somewhere else and 
continue our discussion.

00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:40.080
<i>This guy is unbelievable.</i>

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:42.840
Where should we go?

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:47.050
Oh, uh, I have homework!

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:48.180
Gotta go!

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.460
Oh, hey!

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:50.430
Wait a minute!

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:52.850
Let's talk more about Panda!

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:57.180
You can have this.

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:00.040
Really?

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:01.110
Thank you!

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:02.280
I owe you for a lifetime!

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:04.350
It's okay.

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:06.730
A lifetime is a bit extreme...

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:08.240
I'll cherish it.

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:10.970
I'm really happy.

00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:18.840
Goodbye!

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:22.460
Hey, wait.

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:25.260
<i>Goodbye, my love.</i>

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:28.220
Let's talk about pandas again!

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:31.790
<i>Goodbye, my love!</i>

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:32.710
I'm not...

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:36.760
giving this back, even if you ask!

00:21:50.460 --> 00:21:51.910
Thanks for your hard work.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.110
Iced coffee?

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:54.690
Yeah.

00:21:56.250 --> 00:22:00.040
A half day of manual labor is rough.

00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:04.200
I'm going to ask if they'd make 
it only half of half a day.

00:22:04.910 --> 00:22:08.210
I think it'd be okay to fire you.

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:09.220
Why's that?

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:12.070
Oh, Rin Rin's flowers!

00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:13.390
Could you move them?

00:22:18.160 --> 00:22:19.630
Now, now.

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:22.290
They're pretty flowers.

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.880
Next Time

00:23:58.240 --> 00:23:59.710
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.710 --> 00:24:01.020
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.020 --> 00:24:03.360
Don't you ever feel like you 
wanted to learn a special move,

00:24:03.360 --> 00:24:05.140
even if that meant you'd have to go

00:24:05.140 --> 00:24:06.750
through life-threatening training?

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:07.910
I don't think I do.

00:24:07.910 --> 00:24:10.380
For example, the ability 
to imitate a fax machine.

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:13.300
That's definitely not something I'd go through life-threatening training for.

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:16.640
Penguin's
Melancholy

00:24:14.780 --> 00:24:16.640
Polar Bear, let's end this.

00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:20.240
Next time, Polar Bear's Café vs. 
World Business Satellite.

00:24:20.240 --> 00:24:23.020
Can't you just say, 
"Polar Bear's Café"?

00:24:21.310 --> 00:24:24.720
The Café's Ghost Stories
Panda Runs Away from Home

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:24.720
Enjoy!
